\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.1}{\ignorespaces Overview of the full Luna AI Therapist pipeline: dual-LLM dialogue generation, Zonos TTS synthesis with director-assigned prosody, post-hoc text and speech VA extraction (vad-bert, WavLM), vocal descriptors (librosa), dissonance computation, and the four therapist generation conditions.}}{19}{figure.caption.13}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.2}{\ignorespaces Vocal prosodic descriptor extraction pipeline. Raw audio waveforms from Zonos synthesis are processed via \texttt {librosa} to extract pitch (F0), loudness (RMS), and speaking rate, which are then converted into natural-language contextual descriptors for the Multimodal therapist condition.}}{20}{figure.caption.14}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.1}{\ignorespaces Therapist responses to the same client utterance under two conditions, shown in the demonstration interface. The scripted session uses the identical extraction pipeline and prompts as the main experiments; only the therapist's input metadata differs between conditions.}}{26}{figure.caption.17}%
\contentsline {subfigure}{\numberline {(a)}{\ignorespaces {(a) Baseline (Text-Only) -- The therapist receives only the transcript and takes the client's positive wording at face value.}}}{26}{subfigure.1.1}%
\contentsline {subfigure}{\numberline {(b)}{\ignorespaces {(b) Dissonance-Aware -- The therapist additionally receives the voice analysis: the dissonance flag is raised ($|\delta _V| = 1.05$), and the response gently probes beneath the surface.}}}{26}{subfigure.1.2}%
